hadiths[14]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1271","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, \(The foundation of) Islam is built upon five (pillars)"","" testifying the fact that La ilaha illallah wa anna Muhammad-ar-Rasul-ullah [there is no true god except Allah"","" and Muhammad [ﷺ] is the Messenger of Allah] "","" establishing As- Salat (the prayers)"","" paying Zakat (poor due)"","" the pilgrimage to the House [of Allah (Ka'bah)] "","" and the Saum (fasting) during the month of Ramadan.\"" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] .""
"1272","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) addressed us and said: “O people, Allah has made Hajj obligatory upon you, so perform Hajj.” Then a man said: “Is it every year, O Messenger of Allah?” He was silent, until he said it three times. Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “If I had said yes, it would have been obligatory, and you would not have been able.” Then he said: “Leave me as long as I leave you, for those who were before you perished because of their many questions and their differences over their prophets. If I command you to do something, do as much of it as you can, and if I forbid you to do something, abandon it.” [Muslim]."
"1273","On his authority, he said: The Prophet (ﷺ) was asked which deed is best? He said: “Faith in Allah and His Messenger.” It was said: “Then what?” He said: “Jihad for the sake of Allah.” It was said: “Then what?” He said: “An accepted Hajj” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] “The accepted (Hajj)” is the one in which its performer does not commit any sin."
"1274","On his authority, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: “Whoever performs Hajj and does not commit obscenity or immorality will return as the day his mother gave birth to him.” (Agreed upon)"
"1275","On his authority, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Umrah to Umrah is an expiation for what is between them, and the accepted Hajj has no reward except Paradise” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]"
"1276","On the authority of Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: I said, O Messenger of Allah, we see jihad as the best deed, so should we not strive? He said: “For you (women), the best jihad is an accepted Hajj” [Al-Bukhari]."
"1277","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, There is no day on which Allah sets free more slaves from Hell than He does on the Day of 'Arafah.\"" [Muslim] .""
"1278","On the authority of Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “Umrah in Ramadan is equivalent to an Umrah or Hajj with me.” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]"
"1279","A woman came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and said, Allah's obligation upon His slaves has become obligatory on my father in his old age. My father is very old and incapable of riding. May I perform Hajj on his behalf?\"" He (ﷺ) said"","" \""Yes.\"" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] .""
"1280","And on the authority of Laqit bin Aamir, may Allah be pleased with him, that he came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said: My father is an old man who is unable to perform Hajj or Umrah, nor can he undertake the journey for them. He said: “Perform Hajj on behalf of your father and perform Umrah” [Abu Dawud and Al-Tirmidhi]."
"1281","I was seven years old when I was taken to perform Hajj (pilgrimage). This was during the time the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) performed the Hajjat-ul-Wada' (Farewell Pilgrimage). [Al- Bukhari] ."
"1282","On the authority of Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Prophet (ﷺ) met a rider riding a horse and said: “Who are the people?” They said: Muslims. They said: Who are you? He said: “Messenger of Allah.” Then a woman picked up a boy and said: Is this a Hajj? He said: “Yes, and you will be rewarded” ([Muslim].."
"1283","On the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) performed Hajj on a saddle and she was his companion. [Al-Bukhari]."
"1284","On the authority of Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them, he said: Ukaz, Majnah, and Dhu al-Majaz were markets in the pre-Islamic era, so they considered trading during the seasons to be sinful, so the following verse was revealed: {There is no blame on you if you seek bounty from your Lord} [Al-Baqarah: 198] during the Hajj seasons. ((Narrated by Al-Bukhari).."
